.TH OTPME-POOL 1 "2025-12-29" "OTPme 0.3.0a120" "OTPme Manual"
.SH NAME
otpme-pool \- manage OTPme node pools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B otpme-pool
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIpool\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B otpme-pool
manages node pools in the OTPme system. A pool defines which nodes are used for a share.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Pool Management
.TP
.B add \fIpool\fR
Create a new pool.
.TP
.B del \fIpool\fR
Delete a pool. Asks for confirmation according to the confirmation policy, and warns about shares that use the pool.
.TP
.B show \fR[\fIpool\fR]
Display pool information.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIregex\fR]
List pools, optionally filtered by regex pattern.
.TP
.B enable \fIpool\fR
Enable a disabled pool.
.TP
.B disable \fIpool\fR
Disable a pool without deleting it.
.TP
.B rename \fIpool\fR \fInew_name\fR
Rename a pool.
.TP
.B move \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-acls\fR] \fIpool\fR \fIunit\fR
Move pool to a different unit.
.TP
.B touch \fIpool\fR
Re-index the object to fix potential index problems.
.SS Node Management
.TP
.B add_node \fIpool\fR \fInode\fR
Add a node to the pool.
.TP
.B remove_node \fIpool\fR \fInode\fR
Remove a node from the pool.
.TP
.B list_nodes \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] \fIpool\fR
List nodes in the pool. Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
.SS Policy Management
A \fIpolicy\fR is the name of a policy, not a path.
It is looked for in the site of the pool.
Which policies there are, and what each of them does, is in
.BR otpme\-policy (1).
.PP
Attaching and detaching ask before they change anything; the global option \fB\-f\fR skips the question.
.TP
.B add_policy \fIpool\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Attach a policy to the pool.
.br
A policy has a list of object types it is for; one that does not name \fBpool\fR is refused.
So is a second policy of a type that allows only one per object.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBassign:policy\fR.
.TP
.B remove_policy \fIpool\fR \fIpolicy\fR
Remove a policy from the pool.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBremove:policy\fR, and that one verbatim: a plain \fBremove\fR does not cover it.
Detaching a policy takes away what it enforces, so it must not be cheaper than attaching one.
.TP
.B list_policies \fR[\fB\-\-return\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\-types\fR \fIt1,t2\fR] \fIpool\fR
List the policies attached to the pool.
Use \fB\-\-return\-type\fR to select the attribute returned (\fBname\fR, \fBread_oid\fR, \fBfull_oid\fR, \fBuuid\fR).
Use \fB\-\-policy\-types\fR to list only policies of the given types; these are policy types, not policy names.
.br
Needs the ACL \fBview:policies\fR.
.SS ACL Management
.TP
.B add_acl \fIpool\fR \fIowner_type\fR \fIowner\fR \fIacl\fR
Add an access control entry.
.TP
.B del_acl \fIpool\fR \fIacl\fR
Remove an access control entry.
.TP
.B list_acls \fIpool\fR
Display all ACLs for the pool.
.TP
.B enable_acl_inheritance \fIpool\fR
Enable ACL inheritance from parent objects.
.TP
.B disable_acl_inheritance \fIpool\fR
Disable ACL inheritance.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B description \fIpool\fR \fR[\fIdescription\fR]
Set pool description.
.TP
.B info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIpool\fR \fR[\fIinfo\fR]
Set free-form info text. If \fIinfo\fR is omitted, the current info text is
opened in the editor specified by the \fBEDITOR\fR environment variable.
.TP
.B dump_info \fR[\fB\-\-language\fR \fILANG\fR] \fIpool\fR
Dump the info text to stdout.
.SS Object Changelog
Every change to the object writes an entry: who made it, when, and what was done.
A change can carry a comment of its own, through the global option \fB\-\-changelog\fR.
.PP
An \fIentry_id\fR is the number the listing shows in front of an entry, counted from 0.
.PP
Only the comment of an entry can be changed or removed.
What was done and by whom stays as it is.
.PP
A command that changes something asks first; the global option \fB\-f\fR skips the question.
.TP
.B changelog \fIpool\fR
Show the changelog of the pool.
Needs the ACL \fBview:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B edit_changelog \fIpool\fR \fIentry_id\fR \fIcomment\fR
Set the comment of that entry, or replace the one it has.
Needs the ACL \fBedit:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B del_changelog \fIpool\fR \fIentry_id\fR
Remove the comment of that entry.
The entry itself stays, and an entry without a comment is refused.
Needs the ACL \fBedit:changelog\fR.
.TP
.B clear_changelog \fIpool\fR
Remove every entry of the changelog.
.br
This needs more than the ACL \fBclear:changelog\fR: the config parameter
.B allow_changelog_clearing
has to allow it (see \fBotpme\fR(7)).
It is true by default, but where no value is found at all, clearing is refused.
OTPme asks the token you are signed in with first, then the object.
.SS Import/Export
.TP
.B export \fR[\fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR] \fIpool\fR
Export pool configuration.
.TP
.B remove_orphans \fIpool\fR
Remove orphaned object references.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Display Options
.TP
.B \-a
Show all pools.
.TP
.B \-z \fISIZE\fR
Limit output size.
.TP
.B \-\-fields \fIFIELD1,FIELD2\fR
Display only specified fields.
.TP
.B \-\-node\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of nodes shown.
.TP
.B \-\-token\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of member tokens shown.
.TP
.B \-\-role\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of member roles shown.
.TP
.B \-\-policy\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of policies shown.
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Limit number of items shown per object.
.TP
.B \-\-sort\-by \fIFIELD\fR
Sort output by field.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Output without headers/borders.
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Output as CSV.
.TP
.B \-\-csv\-sep \fISEP\fR
CSV separator character.
.SS General Options
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-acls
Preserve ACLs when moving pool.
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIPASS\fR
Password for encrypting exports.
.PP
Global options are available for all commands. See
.BR otpme (1)
for details.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B otpme-pool add europe
Create a pool
.TP
.B otpme-pool add_node europe node-eu-1
Add a node to the pool
.TP
.B otpme-pool list_nodes europe
List nodes in the pool
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/otpme/
OTPme data directory
